# Data conversion between bit and pebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and pebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.0000PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.0000PiB; backward, converting 1PiB to 9007199254740992b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5PiB yields 13510798882111488.0b. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(PiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(PiB))
backward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(backward_whole->to(b))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.0000PiB
0.0000PiB
9007199254740992b
13510798882111488.0b

<<< stderr
